														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3774948">
									

<p>As I said in chat, I enjoyed this scip. You were inspired by a rather old concept (infinite rooms/topographical glitches) that's been done well before (SCP-184) and you managed to put your own fresh spin on it. There easily could have been a few collapsibles dedicated to exploration logs but you kept the creativity contained in a series of journal logs (which do a good job of creeping me out, personally).</p>
<p>Things I liked about this:</p>
<ul>
<li>Your own invention for the sake of the scip: the Relative Positioning System (RPS)</li>
<li>The &quot;not-Josef&quot; situation, which is much deeper than at first glance (infinite Josefs finding infinite not-Josefs)</li>
<li>The exploration team found in the maze of rooms: where did they come from? Their existence is intriguing and frankly a bit scary. Definitely captures some of the fear of the unknown horror found in Series I (having a lack of information that is disseminated in just the right way to evoke maximum fear).</li>
</ul>

							</div>

